            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0530" n="442" xml:id="pg442"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Newberry to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-12-13"><hi rendition="#italic">December 13, 1890</hi></date>.
                        (Received December 30.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 214.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I received this morning a note from the
                    minister for foreign affairs, a copy and translation of which is inclosed, also
                    copy of my reply, which refers to the late occupation of missionary property by
                    the Spaniards at Ponape. This note is in answer to mine of November 26, to the
                    said minister, copy of which I inclosed to the Department in my No. 205, of
                    November 26. As Minister Grubb arrives to-morrow, I will lay the facts and
                    correspondence before him as soon as convenient.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.;</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. R. Newberry</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d367-a1.xml" xpointer="d367-a1"/>
